{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,280p' src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc; sed -n '340,510p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; sed -n '910,1005p' test/dao/stream/ws_project_cross_node_test.cljs; rg -n 'core-module|pr-str|sort|canonical' src/cljc/dao/jing* src/cljc/yang/core* src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.vm.encoder\n  \"The encoder observer: the `run-on-stream` consumer the composition\n   attaches over the program medium so the semantic VM never sees a map AST\n   or a datom batch (§9.1, `docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`).\n\n   It is a stage in its own right, not a loader arm. The composition hands\n   its session the row medium's writer as the consumer; `run-on-stream`\n   hands it each observed program batch; it projects the batch to the\n   canonical row set and forwards it — appends it to the row medium. The\n   evaluator observer the composition attaches to that row medium\n   independently is the next stage: the two never call each other, they\n   communicate through the row medium alone, so compiler and evaluator stay\n   independently attachable (no direct function-to-function coupling\n   without a stream boundary).\n\n   Projection is this boundary's one job (§9.1): the map AST the frontends\n   emit projects directly through `yin.vm/ast->semantic-bytecode`; a\n   `:yin/*` datom batch projects through the explicit datom→row adapter\n   below — §7.1's projection path, for media that carry datoms.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(defn source-envelope\n  \"Construct the provenance-bearing input value ruled by D4. The admitting\n   composition supplies its program medium's logical identity and mints a\n   fresh batch token before append. `members` is ordered and `root` selects\n   the member the evaluator runs. The constructor validates but never mints:\n   retries of an unaccepted staged append must retain the caller's token.\"\n  ([source-medium batch-token members]\n   (source-envelope source-medium batch-token members 0))\n  ([source-medium batch-token members root]\n   (let [envelope {:yin/source-medium source-medium\n                   :yin/batch-token batch-token\n                   :yin/batch (vec members)\n                   :yin/root root}]\n     ;; Validating the root origin validates the two opaque coordinates too.\n     (when-not (and (integer? root) (<= 0 root) (< root (count members)))\n       (throw (ex-info \"Malformed source batch envelope\"\n                       {:rule :batch-envelope, :envelope envelope})))\n     (vm/source-origin source-medium batch-token root)\n     envelope)))\n\n\n(defn- datom-child-places\n  [get-attr eid]\n  (case (get-attr eid :yin/type)\n    :lambda [[3 (get-attr eid :yin/body)]]\n    :application (concat [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/operator)]]\n                         (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n                                      (get-attr eid :yin/operands)))\n    :if [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/test)]\n         [3 (get-attr eid :yin/consequent)]\n         [4 (get-attr eid :yin/alternate)]]\n    :dao.stream.apply/call\n    (map-indexed (fn [i child] [[3 i] child])\n                 (get-attr eid :yin/operands))\n    :stream/put [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/target)]\n                 [3 (get-attr eid :yin/val-node)]]\n    (:stream/cursor :stream/next :stream/close)\n    [[2 (get-attr eid :yin/source)]]\n    :vm/resume [[3 (get-attr eid :yin/val-node)]]\n    []))\n\n\n(defn datom-entity-occurrences\n  \"The §9.1 datom adapter's path/entity relation for one admitted member:\n   `[member-index path entity-id]` once per structural occurrence. Shared\n   entities therefore appear at every path while retaining one entity\n   identity, which is the information U16's harvest catalogue derives from.\n   Cyclic or dangling legacy graphs fail at this boundary.\"\n  [datoms member-index]\n  (let [{:keys [root-id get-attr error]} (vm/index-datoms datoms)]\n    (when error\n      (throw (ex-info \"Cannot adapt a datom batch with a dangling root\" error)))\n    (when (nil? root-id)\n      (throw (ex-info \"Cannot adapt a datom batch with no root\"\n                      {:rule :root})))\n    (letfn [(walk\n              [eid path active]\n              (when (contains? active eid)\n                (throw (ex-info \"Cannot adapt a cyclic datom AST\"\n                                {:rule :cycle, :entity eid, :path path})))\n              (when (nil? (get-attr eid :yin/type))\n                (throw (ex-info \"Cannot adapt a dangling datom AST reference\"\n                                {:rule :dangling-ref, :entity eid, :path path})))\n              (into [[member-index path eid]]\n                    (mapcat (fn [[step child]]\n                              (walk child (conj path step) (conj active eid))))\n                    (datom-child-places get-attr eid)))]\n      (vec (walk root-id [] #{})))))\n\n\n(defn datoms->rows\n  \"§7.1's projection path as an explicit adapter: a `:yin/*` datom batch\n   reconstructs its map AST (`vm/datoms->ast`), then projects like every\n   other batch — the datom→row half of the §9.1 codec pair.\"\n  [datoms]\n  (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode (vm/datoms->ast datoms)))\n\n\n(defn- project-member\n  [member origin member-index]\n  (cond\n    (and (map? member) (contains? member :type))\n    (let [tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode member)]\n      (merge {:tree tree, :entity-occurrences []}\n             (vm/ast-side-tables member tree origin)))\n\n    (and (map? member) (contains? member :root) (contains? member :rows))\n    {:tree member, :source-positions [], :frontend-metadata [],\n     :entity-occurrences []}\n\n    (sequential? member)\n    (let [datoms (vec member)\n          ast (vm/datoms->ast datoms)\n          tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)]\n      (merge {:tree tree\n              :entity-occurrences (datom-entity-occurrences datoms member-index)}\n             (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\n\n    :else\n    (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported source batch member\"\n                    {:rule :batch-member, :member member,\n                     :member-index member-index}))))\n\n\n(defn- project-envelope\n  [{:yin/keys [source-medium batch-token batch root] :as envelope}]\n  (when-not (and (vector? batch)\n                 (seq batch)\n                 (integer? root)\n                 (<= 0 root)\n                 (< root (count batch)))\n    (throw (ex-info \"Malformed source batch envelope\"\n                    {:rule :batch-envelope, :envelope envelope})))\n  (let [projected (mapv (fn [j member]\n                          (project-member member\n                                          (vm/source-origin source-medium\n                                                            batch-token j)\n                                          j))\n                        (range) batch)]\n    (assoc envelope\n           :yin/batch (mapv :tree projected)\n           :yin/source-positions (into [] (mapcat :source-positions) projected)\n           :yin/frontend-metadata (into [] (mapcat :frontend-metadata) projected)\n           :yin/entity-occurrences (into [] (mapcat :entity-occurrences) projected))))\n\n\n(defn project\n  \"One program-medium batch to its canonical row set `{:root id, :rows …}`\n   (§6.1). A batch that is neither a map AST nor a datom batch is a defect\n   of the medium and throws here, at the boundary, naming where it failed.\"\n  [batch]\n  (cond\n    (and (map? batch) (contains? batch :yin/batch))\n    (project-envelope batch)\n\n    (map? batch) (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode batch)\n    :else (datoms->rows batch)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The macro expander's input batch (yin.vm.macro.md §2.1, §10.2)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- definition-name\n  \"The name of a `(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)` AST node (§2.2), else nil.\"\n  [{:keys [type operator operands]}]\n  (when (and (= :application type)\n             (= :variable (:type operator))\n             (= 'yin/def (:name operator))\n             (= 2 (count operands))\n             (= :literal (:type (first operands)))\n             (symbol? (:value (first operands))))\n    (:value (first operands))))\n\n\n(defn- ast-children\n  \"`[[path-suffix child] ...]` of one AST node in grammar order. A suffix\n   holds one coordinate: the full-row position of a `node` slot or\n   `[position i]` of a `nodes` child, as in its canonical row (§2.1).\"\n  [node]\n  (apply concat\n         (map-indexed (fn [i [field kind]]\n                        (let [pos (+ i 2)]\n                          (case kind\n                            :node [[[pos] (get node field)]]\n                            :nodes (map-indexed (fn [k c] [[[pos k]] c])\n                                                (get node field))\n                            nil)))\n                      (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node)))))\n\n\n(defn- declaration-order\n  \"§3.5's declaration order for one node's children: for an application\n   whose operator is a lambda, the operands left to right and then the\n   lambda body (two coordinates below the application); otherwise grammar\n   order.\"\n  [node]\n  (let [places (ast-children node)]\n    (if (and (= :application (:type node)) (= :lambda (:type (:operator node))))\n      (concat (rest places) [[[2 3] (:body (:operator node))]])\n      places)))\n\n\n(defn- definition-occurrences\n  \"Every definition occurrence of one member AST as `{:path p :declared? b}`,\n   in source declaration order. A declared occurrence is one whose value is\n   a lambda the frontend flagged `:macro?`.\"\n  [ast]\n  (letfn [(walk [node path]\n            (concat (when (definition-name node)\n                      [{:path path,\n                        :declared? (boolean (:macro? (second (:operands node))))}])\n                    (mapcat (fn [[suffix child]] (walk child (into path suffix)))\n                            (declaration-order node))))]\n    (vec (walk ast []))))\n\n\n(defn- member-ast\n  [member]\n  (cond (and (map? member) (contains? member :type)) member\n        (sequential? member) (vm/datoms->ast (vec member))\n        :else (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported program batch member\"\n                              {:rule :batch-member, :member member}))))\n\n\n(def ^:private call-site-key\n  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence\n   contract C1 (`yang.clojure`), enforced at this boundary but not\n   owned by it.\"\n  :yang/call-site)\n\n\n(defn- marked-call-sites\n  \"The `[path value]` of every node of map AST `ast` carrying the C1\n   key, walked by the row grammar. Literal payloads are data, never\n   syntax, and are not walked. Member ASTs are already projected by the\n   time this runs, so every tag is a grammar tag.\"\n  [ast]\n  (letfn [(walk\n            [node path]\n            (into (if (contains? node call-site-key)\n                    [[path (get node call-site-key)]]\n                    [])\n                  (mapcat (fn [[j [field kind]]]\n                            (let [pos (+ j 2)\n                                  value (get node field)]\n                              (case kind\n                                :node (walk value (conj path pos))\n                                :nodes (mapcat (fn [[i child]]\n                                                 (walk child\n                                                       (conj path [pos i])))\n                                               (map-indexed vector value))\n                                nil)))\n                          (map-indexed vector\n                                       (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar\n                                            (:type node))))))]\n    (walk ast [])))\n\n\n(defn- check-call-site-claim!\n  \"Refuse a batch member whose C1 markers do not exactly cover its\n   projected tree, naming the failed `:rule`: canonical-row production\n   must not silently drop a frontend's coverage claim. The claim is\n   checked root-relatively — admission origins belong to the admitting\n   expander, not to this projection. A member carrying no markers\n   makes no claim and passes; the executed tree's table is finalized\n   after expansion, over the final rows. Answers true when the member\n   claimed coverage (it passed the check), false when it carried no\n   markers — one verdict per member, so the selected member's own\n   verdict, never a sibling's, decides whether the expander finalizes\n   its side table.\"\n  [ast tree]\n  (let [marked (marked-call-sites ast)]\n    (if (seq marked)\n      (do (doseq [[path value] marked]\n            (when (not= 1 value)\n         (cond\n           (::thrown task)\n           [w [:thrown (::thrown task)] response (observed (::resumed task))]\n\n           (and (vm/blocked? task) (< (:now w) limit))\n           (let [{:keys [pair dht admission] :as served}\n                 (link/serve {:pair pair,\n                              :source src,\n                              :dht (:reader w),\n                              :admission adm})\n                 admitted (when interp\n                            (admission/serve\n                              {:interpreter interp,\n                               :policy (:admission src),\n                               :context (admission/context {})}\n                              link/serve-budget))\n                 w (between (step-world (assoc w :reader dht)) served)]\n             (recur w\n                    (run task)\n                    pair\n                    admission\n                    (if admitted (:interpreter admitted) interp)))\n\n           :else\n           [w\n            [(vm/halted? task) (vm/blocked? task)\n             (render/output (vm/value task))]\n            response\n            (observed task)]))))))\n\n\n(defn- source\n  \"The reader's DHT link source declaring the public keys `publics`, its\n   in-process admission interpreter trusting the principals of the\n   public keys `trusted` -- none in process when `trusted` is nil.\"\n  [publics trusted]\n  (link/composition\n    {:dht? true,\n     :principals publics,\n     :admission (when trusted\n                  {:trusted (set (map sign/principal trusted))})}))\n\n\n(defn- on-every-vm\n  \"Thread `w` through `run-over-dht` on every vector backend: `[w {backend\n   [outcome last-response observation]}]`.\"\n  [w pk src]\n  (reduce (fn [[w acc] k]\n            (let [[w outcome response seen] (run-over-dht w k pk src)]\n              [w (assoc acc k [outcome response seen])]))\n          [w {}]\n          (keys h/backends)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The acceptance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- first-difference\n  \"The first key of the artifacts `a` and `b` (`fixture/parse`'s data)\n   whose values differ, with the blob addresses only one holds or holds\n   other bytes at; nil when they are equal.\"\n  [a b]\n  (when (not= a b)\n    (let [blobs (fn [x y]\n                  (sort (map str (remove #(= (get x %) (get y %))\n                                         (keys x)))))]\n      {:keys (vec (sort (map str (filter #(not= (get a %) (get b %))\n                                         (distinct (concat (keys a)\n                                                           (keys b))))))),\n       :blobs-differ (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs a) (:blobs b)))),\n       :blobs-only-here (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs b) (:blobs a))))})))\n\n\n(defn- this-host-publishes-the-artifact\n  [artifact-lines]\n  (testing \"this host's own publication of the committed packets is the\n            JVM's artifact: same manifests, blobs and envelopes\"\n    (let [{:keys [lines refused]} (fixture/generate)]\n      (is (nil? refused) (pr-str refused))\n      (when lines\n        (is (nil? (first-difference (fixture/parse artifact-lines)\n                                    (fixture/parse lines))))))))\n\n\n(defn- publish-world\n  \"Publisher `A` at mesh port 1, plain peers at 2 and 3, a reader at 4,\n   `A` and the reader with `py` installed: `A`'s node serves the\n   artifact's guest blobs as they are and its first index (py, m, k and\n   t named by `A`), which the reader loads.\"\n  [artifact]\n  (let [net (mesh/mesh)\n        installed (fixture/installed-py)\n        pub (node-at net 1 [2 3] true installed)\n        put! (:put-bytes-fn (dht/store pub))\n        w {:net net,\n           :pub pub,\n           :reader (node-at net 4 [2 3 1] false\n                            (merge installed (fixture/installed-pysp))),\n           :peers (into {} (map (fn [p] [p (peer-node net p)])) [2 3]),\n           :now 0,\n           :events []}]\n    (testing \"every node's installed py is the artifact's\"\n      (is (= (:py artifact) (:address @h/published))))\n    (run! (fn [[address bs]] (put! address bs))\n          (sort-by (comp str key) (:blobs artifact)))\n    (first (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :own])))))\n\n\n(def ^:private nothing-ran\n  \"A refused import's observation: no line printed and no guest install\n   child; `yang.call` and `py` are the two runtime install children.\"\n  {:output [], :guests #{}, :children 2})\n\n\n(defn- observes\n  \"Assert each key of the observation `expected` of backend `k` on its\n   own, so a failure names the key.\"\n  [k expected seen]\n  (doseq [[key v] expected]\n    (is (= v (get seen key)) (str k \" \" key))))\n\n\n(defn- imports-over-the-dht\n  [w artifact src]\n  (testing \"a JVM-published pym.m imports over the DHT, parserless, with\n            the in-store linked run's output and CPython's\"\n    (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :d]) src)]\n      (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n        (is (= [true false {:py/out [\"m-body\" \"7\"], :py/exception nil}]\n               outcome)\n            (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n        (testing \"and the observation sees the same run\"\n          ;; The linked task installs `py`, the shared `yang.call`\n          ;; dispatcher, then the guest module.\n          (observes k {:output [\"m-body\" \"7\"], :guests #{\"pym.m\"},\n                       :children 3}\n                    seen)))\n      (testing \"and t delivers k, its pinned import, by name\"\n        (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :tt])\n                                       src)]\n          (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n            (is (= [true false\n                    {:py/out [\"k-body\" \"t-sees 3\" \"t-done\"],\n                     :py/exception nil}]\n                   outcome)\n                (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n            (observes k {:guests #{\"pym.k\" \"pym.t\"}} seen))\n          w)))))\n\n\n(defn- republished-dependency-is-refused\n  [w artifact src]\n  (let [k1 (get-in artifact [:units \"k\"])\n        k2 (get-in artifact [:republished \"k\"])\n        [w _] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :republish]))]\n    (testing \"a republished dependency: t pinned k's first address, k now\n              names another; the link server delivers k2, but the engine\n              refuses receive as a pin mismatch, raising ImportError in t\"\n      (is (not= k1 k2))\n      (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :tt])\n                                     src)]\n        (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n          (is (= [true false\n                  {:py/out [],\n                   :py/exception\n                   {:type \"ImportError\",\n                    :args [\"Cannot import module 'k': linker refused