{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc '/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff --stat f4df9893 b1b9abae; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff f4df9893 b1b9abae -- src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc'","aggregated_output":" src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc           |  253 ++++++-\n src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc   |    5 +-\n src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc         |    7 +-\n src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc         |   46 +-\n src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc     |   16 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc                 |   14 +\n src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc         |  129 +++-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc          |   17 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc  |   46 +-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc  |  305 ++++++++-\n src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc           |  703 +++++++++++++++++---\n test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | 1212 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n test/yang/core/call_test.cljc        |    9 +-\n test/yin/vm/encoder_test.cljc        |    7 +-\n 14 files changed, 2595 insertions(+), 174 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\nindex 42a3bead..54d1a80b 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc\n@@ -107,8 +107,9 @@\n \n (def module-uast\n   \"The module tree: one wide application over the definitions, so every\n-   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level.\"\n-  (core/module-tree module-definitions []))\n+   sibling and runtime key read is discharged at module level. C1\n+   finalized, like every production `yang.clojure` tree.\"\n+  (yang/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n \n \n (def module-exports\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc\nindex f1414ddb..da597c68 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc\n@@ -18,7 +18,8 @@\n      (f a ...)         -> :application\n      any other value   -> :literal\"\n   (:require\n-    [yang.tails :as tails]))\n+    [yang.tails :as tails]\n+    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n \n \n (defn lit\n@@ -105,3 +106,46 @@\n   \"`yang.tails/mark-tails`: the lowering marks its tree with the same\n    function a rewriting stage recomputes the marks with.\"\n   tails/mark-tails)\n+\n+\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;;\n+;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a produced tree carries the\n+;; reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with version value `1`\n+;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\n+;; from canonical rows and emits it into the frontend-metadata side table\n+;; as `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, where the first\n+;; three coordinates are the site id. The key carries no callee identity,\n+;; source arity, or ambient classification. It is distinct from\n+;; `:yang/site`, the safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata.\n+;; Dedicated node kinds (`:dao.stream.apply/call`, stream and\n+;; continuation nodes) are not `:application` nodes and are never marked.\n+;; The walk lives here, beside the other shared tree transforms, so every\n+;; frontend's module trees finalize the same way; `yang.clojure` owns the\n+;; contract's validation over canonical rows.\n+\n+(defn annotate-call-sites\n+  \"The finished map AST `node` with `:yang/call-site 1` on every\n+   `:application` node, at every depth the row grammar knows. Literal\n+   payloads are data, never syntax, and are not walked. Marking is\n+   idempotent and preserves node metadata and every other key, so\n+   canonical rows, roots, and executable outcomes are unchanged.\"\n+  [node]\n+  (let [tag (:type node)\n+        slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar tag)]\n+    (when-not slots\n+      (throw (ex-info \"Unknown AST node type\" {:type tag, :node node})))\n+    (let [walked (reduce (fn [n [field kind]]\n+                           (case kind\n+                             :node (update n field annotate-call-sites)\n+                             :nodes (update n field\n+                                            (fn [children]\n+                                              (mapv annotate-call-sites\n+                                                    children)))\n+                             n))\n+                         node\n+                         slots)]\n+      (cond-> walked\n+        (= :application tag) (assoc :yang/call-site 1)))))\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\nindex c5dc7161..f706f033 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc\n@@ -90,6 +90,131 @@\n    linker/stack-format linker/register-format])\n \n \n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;;\n+;; A module whose frontend finalized its tree (`:yang/call-site 1` on\n+;; every final `:application` occurrence) publishes its frontend-metadata\n+;; side table with its manifest: the manifest keeps schema 1 (a manifest\n+;; address names code) and gains the optional `:yin.module/call-sites`\n+;; reference `{table record}` — the module closure follows manifest\n+;; references, so only a referenced table travels with the module\n+;; through transfer. The reverse record names the tree root, the\n+;; publication's recorded admission origin, and the table's address; it\n+;; cannot name the manifest (the manifest references it, so the two\n+;; addresses would be circular), and custody runs one way, from the\n+;; manifest forward. The publication's origin is an ADMISSION identity\n+;; (design §2.1): a token the composition pins explicitly, draws from\n+;; a composition-owned scope object, or — by default — has derived\n+;; from the publication specification's own durable identity; no\n+;; counter or other mutable state lives in this namespace. The token\n+;; is persisted in the record and retrieved from the record, never\n+;; reconstructed from the tree's content. The publisher\n+;; extracts the markers from the map AST, refuses the\n+;; publication when they do not exactly cover the canonical tree's\n+;; application occurrences — or when a marker's value is not version 1 —\n+;; and otherwise materializes the table and its record into the same\n+;; handle. A module with no markers makes no claim and publishes exactly\n+;; as before.\n+\n+(defn admission-scope\n+  \"An admission scope for `publish-module!`'s `:yin.link.publish/scope`\n+   option. `id` names this publisher — a durable, caller-chosen\n+   identity (a string or keyword) that distinguishes this publisher's\n+   admissions from every other publisher's; a publisher that must not\n+   collide with its own past runs takes a fresh `id` per run. The\n+   returned scope object OWNS the publication ordinal counter, so no\n+   counter lives in this namespace (no hidden global state): two\n+   publications through one scope draw consecutive ordinals, and two\n+   independent scopes publishing identical specifications still yield\n+   distinct admission identities, because their `id`s differ.\"\n+  [id]\n+  {:yin.link.publish/scope-id id\n+   :yin.link.publish/ordinal (atom 0)})\n+\n+(defn- scope-admission-token\n+  \"The admission token a scope object draws for one publication: the\n+   scope's own `id` plus the ordinal the scope's counter assigns. The\n+   counter lives in the caller-owned scope object, never here.\"\n+  [{:yin.link.publish/keys [scope-id ordinal]}]\n+  ;; pr-str keeps the value's full identity — a keyword's namespace, a\n+  ;; string's quoting, a symbol's name — so distinct caller-chosen ids\n+  ;; (:a/publisher, :b/publisher, \"publisher\") never mint the same token\n+  (keyword \"yin.vm.linker.publish.scope\"\n+           (str (pr-str scope-id) \"#\" (swap! ordinal inc))))\n+\n+(defn- spec-admission-token\n+  \"The default admission token: derived deterministically from the\n+   publication specification's own durable identity — the module name\n+   and the content address of its compiled tree — never from hidden\n+   mutable state. Two publications of the same specification therefore\n+   answer the same admission identity (an idempotent re-publication is\n+   the same recorded admission), and distinct specifications never\n+   share one, in this or any other publisher process. A composition\n+   that admits the same specification more than once as separate\n+   admissions passes an `:yin.link.publish/scope` (or an explicit\n+   `:yin.link.publish/admission`) so the admissions stay distinct.\"\n+  [{:keys [name]} tree]\n+  (keyword \"yin.vm.linker.publish.publication\"\n+           (str name \"::\" (:root tree))))\n+\n+(defn- publication-origin\n+  \"The occurrence origin of the publication admission `token` names:\n+   the publisher's own medium, the explicit admission token, member 0.\n+   `token` is the publication's admission identity — the\n+   `:yin.link.publish/admission` option when the composition pins one,\n+   the `:yin.link.publish/scope` option's next drawn token when the\n+   composition scopes the publisher, otherwise the token derived from\n+   the publication specification's own durable identity. The origin is\n+   an admission event's identity, not a function of the tree's content\n+   alone: it is persisted in the side record at publication time and\n+   retrieved from that record; nothing ever reconstructs it from the\n+   root.\"\n+  [token]\n+  [:source :yin.vm.linker.publish/publish token 0])\n+\n+\n+(defn- claims-call-sites?\n+  \"True when map AST `ast` carries the C1 key anywhere. A hit inside a\n+   literal payload is data, not a claim: extraction then finds no\n+   markers and the module publishes unannotated, as it should.\"\n+  [ast]\n+  (boolean (some #(= :yang/call-site %) (tree-seq coll? seq ast))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- call-site-claim\n+  \"The C1 claim `ast` makes over its canonical `tree`: nil when it\n+   carries no markers; `{:origin o :rows [...]}` in printed-row order\n+   when the extracted markers exactly cover the tree's eligible\n+   application occurrences; `{:missing [...] :extra [...]}` when they\n+   do not; `{:unsupported-version v :path p}` when a marker's value is\n+   not version 1 — a claim rejection, never a silent acceptance of a\n+   table a retriever would read as version 1.\"\n+  [ast tree admission]\n+  (when (claims-call-sites? ast)\n+    (let [origin (publication-origin admission)\n+          extracted (filter #(= :yang/call-site (nth % 3))\n+                            (:frontend-metadata\n+                              (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\n+          eligible (into #{}\n+                         (map (fn [[r p]] [origin r p]))\n+                         (vm/application-occurrences tree))\n+          marked (into #{}\n+                       (map (fn [[o r p _ _]] [o r p]))\n+                       extracted)]\n+      (or (when-let [[v p] (some (fn [row]\n+                                   (let [v (nth row 4)]\n+                                     (when (not (and (integer? v) (= 1 v)))\n+                                       [v (subvec row 0 3)])))\n+                                 extracted)]\n+            {:unsupported-version v, :path p})\n+          (if (= eligible marked)\n+            {:origin origin, :rows (vec (sort-by pr-str extracted))}\n+            {:missing (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove marked eligible))),\n+             :extra (vec (sort-by pr-str (remove eligible marked)))})))))\n+\n+\n (defn link-local\n   \"Link `format`'s image through the manifest `address` over `handle`'s\n    own content, `:verifying` with discharge deferred, as a serving\n@@ -138,7 +263,25 @@\n                 (sort-by (fn [[n _]] (str n)) requires)))\n         fp (when (and tree (not defect) (not requirement)\n                       (not= :refused (:status tree)))\n-             (footprint handle (assoc spec :tree tree)))]\n+             (footprint handle (assoc spec :tree tree)))\n+        ;; a C1 claim is validated before anything is written: a module\n+        ;; whose markers do not cover its tree is never published as\n+        ;; though it did. One publication is one admission event\n+        ;; (design §2.1): the admission identity is pinned explicitly by\n+        ;; the composition when it supplies `:yin.link.publish/admission`,\n+        ;; drawn from the composition's own scope object when it supplies\n+        ;; `:yin.link.publish/scope`, and otherwise derived from the\n+        ;; specification's own durable identity — no counter lives in\n+        ;; this namespace. Either way it is persisted in the side record\n+        ;; and retrieved from there\n+        admission (or (:yin.link.publish/admission opts)\n+                      (when-let [scope (:yin.link.publish/scope opts)]\n+                        (scope-admission-token scope))\n+                      (when tree (spec-admission-token spec tree)))\n+        claim (when (and tree (not defect) (not requirement)\n+                         (not= :refused (:status tree))\n+                         (not= :refused (:status fp)))\n+                (call-site-claim ast tree admission))]\n     (cond\n       undefined\n       (refusal :yin.link.publish/undefined-export {:export undefined})\n@@ -152,6 +295,16 @@\n \n       (= :refused (:status fp)) fp\n \n+      ;; dispatch on the key's PRESENCE, not its truthiness: a marker\n+      ;; whose value is present but not the integer 1 — nil or false\n+      ;; included — carries :unsupported-version nil/false, and its\n+      ;; reason is the unsupported version, never incomplete coverage\n+      (and claim (contains? claim :unsupported-version))\n+      (refusal :yin.link.publish/unsupported-call-site-version claim)\n+\n+      (and claim (not (:rows claim)))\n+      (refusal :yin.link.publish/incomplete-call-site-coverage claim)\n+\n       :else\n       (let [tree-address (vm/materialize-tree! handle tree)\n             sem-vector (:vector (linearize/project-rows tree))\n@@ -167,28 +320,45 @@\n                      handle\n                      (assoc (ledger/derive-record input output)\n                             :yin.ledger/profile profile)))\n-            manifest {:yin.module/name name\n-                      :yin.module/schema linker/manifest-schema\n-                      :yin.module/contracts\n-                      {:yin.ast/code vm/ast-contract\n-                       :yin.semantic/code vm/semantic-contract\n-                       :yin.debruijn.code vm/stack-contract\n-                       :yin.debruijn.register vm/register-contract}\n-                      :yin.module/tree tree-address\n-                      :yin.module/derivations\n-                      {:yin.semantic/code (mint tree-address sem ledger/lowering-profile)\n-                       :yin.debruijn.code\n-                       (mint sem h linker/stack-lowering-profile)\n-                       :yin.debruijn.register\n-                       (mint sem r linker/register-lowering-profile)}\n-                      :yin.module/index {:yin.debruijn.code h-address\n-                                         :yin.debruijn.register r-address}\n-                      :yin.module/exports (set exports)\n-                      :yin.module/requires (or requires {})\n-                      :yin.module/primitives\n-                      (into {} (map (fn [[n p]] [n (:yin.k/profile p)])\n-                                    primitives))\n-                      :yin.module/footprint fp}\n+            ;; the C1 side table and its reverse record, materialized\n+            ;; BEFORE the manifest so the manifest can reference them:\n+            ;; the module closure follows manifest references, so only a\n+            ;; referenced table travels with the module through transfer\n+            call-sites (when (:rows claim)\n+                         (let [table (jing/materialize! handle (:rows claim))\n+                               record {:yang.call-site/version 1\n+                                       :yang.call-site/root tree-address\n+                                       :yang.call-site/origin (:origin claim)\n+                                       :yang.call-site/table table}]\n+                           {:record (jing/materialize! handle record)\n+                            :table table\n+                            :origin (:origin claim)\n+                            :root (:root tree)}))\n+            manifest (cond-> {:yin.module/name name\n+                              :yin.module/schema linker/manifest-schema\n+                              :yin.module/contracts\n+                              {:yin.ast/code vm/ast-contract\n+                               :yin.semantic/code vm/semantic-contract\n+                               :yin.debruijn.code vm/stack-contract\n+                               :yin.debruijn.register vm/register-contract}\n+                              :yin.module/tree tree-address\n+                              :yin.module/derivations\n+                              {:yin.semantic/code (mint tree-address sem ledger/lowering-profile)\n+                               :yin.debruijn.code\n+                               (mint sem h linker/stack-lowering-profile)\n+                               :yin.debruijn.register\n+                               (mint sem r linker/register-lowering-profile)}\n+                              :yin.module/index {:yin.debruijn.code h-address\n+                                                 :yin.debruijn.register r-address}\n+                              :yin.module/exports (set exports)\n+                              :yin.module/requires (or requires {})\n+                              :yin.module/primitives\n+                              (into {} (map (fn [[n p]] [n (:yin.k/profile p)])\n+                                            primitives))\n+                              :yin.module/footprint fp}\n+                       call-sites (assoc :yin.module/call-sites\n+                                         {:table (:table call-sites)\n+                                          :record (:record call-sites)}))\n             address (jing/materialize! handle manifest)\n             walked (closure/walk handle address opts)]\n         (if (not= :complete (:yin.link.closure/outcome walked))\n@@ -201,23 +371,98 @@\n                                                 (select-keys opts\n                                                              [:bounds]))]))\n                             code-formats)]\n-            {:address address :manifest manifest\n-             :identities {:yin.semantic/code sem\n-                          :yin.debruijn.code sem\n-                          :yin.debruijn.register sem}\n-             :checksums {:yin.debruijn.code h :yin.debruijn.register r}\n-             :links links}))))))\n+            (cond-> {:address address :manifest manifest\n+                     :identities {:yin.semantic/code sem\n+                                  :yin.debruijn.code sem\n+                                  :yin.debruijn.register sem}\n+                     :checksums {:yin.debruijn.code h\n+                                 :yin.debruijn.register r}\n+                     :links links}\n+              call-sites (assoc :call-sites call-sites))))))))\n \n \n (defn publish-module!\n   \"Mint all four code formats, derivation records, and one schema-1 manifest.\n    `opts` `{:bounds {...}}` are the composition bounds (section 4.2 step\n    2) of every closure walk and local link the publication runs, every\n-   bound left out taking `linker/default-bounds`.\"\n+   bound left out taking `linker/default-bounds`. `opts` may also pin\n+   the publication's admission identity explicitly\n+   (`:yin.link.publish/admission`) or scope it — a scope object from\n+   `admission-scope` under `:yin.link.publish/scope`, whose counter the\n+   caller owns; without either, the admission identity is derived from\n+   the specification's own durable identity, so re-publishing the same\n+   specification is the same recorded admission.\"\n   ([handle spec] (publish-module! handle spec nil))\n   ([handle spec opts] (publish-closure! handle spec opts)))\n \n \n+(defn- stored-tree\n+  \"The canonical row tree stored under `root` in `handle`, rebuilt\n+   from its individually materialized rows (`vm/materialize-tree!`\n+   stores each row body under its own address), or nil when a reached\n+   row is absent.\"\n+  [handle root]\n+  (loop [queue [root]\n+         rows {}]\n+    (if (empty? queue)\n+      {:root root, :rows rows}\n+      (let [address (first queue)\n+            body (jing/get handle address nil)]\n+        (if-not (vector? body)\n+          nil\n+          (let [row (into [address] body)\n+                kids (into []\n+                           (mapcat (fn [[j [_ kind]]]\n+                                     (let [pos (+ j 2)]\n+                                       (case kind\n+                                         :node [(nth row pos)]\n+                                         :nodes (nth row pos)\n+                                         nil))))\n+                           (map-indexed vector\n+                                        (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar\n+                                             (nth row 1))))]\n+            (recur (into (subvec queue 1)\n+                         (remove #(contains? rows %) kids))\n+                   (assoc rows address row))))))))\n+\n+\n+(defn published-call-site-table\n+  \"The C1 side table the module whose manifest is at `address` in\n+   `handle` claims: `{:origin o :root r :rows [...] :tree tree}` with\n+   the rows exactly as stored and the module's canonical tree, or nil\n+   when the module made no C1 claim. The manifest references the table\n+   and its reverse record (`:yin.module/call-sites`), so the reference —\n+   not a recomputation — is what is resolved here: the rows are fetched\n+   from the referenced table address and the ORIGIN is the one the\n+   record RECORDED at publication (`:yang.call-site/origin`, held to be\n+   a well-formed occurrence origin), beside the record's version, the\n+   manifest's own tree, and the referenced table. Nothing reconstructs\n+   an origin from content: a replay of this retrieval answers the\n+   recorded admission identity, and no other module's admission can be\n+   confused with it.\"\n+  [handle address]\n+  (let [manifest (jing/get handle address nil)\n+        call-sites (:yin.module/call-sites manifest)]\n+    (when (and (map? manifest) (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n+               (map? call-sites) (jing/segment-address? (:table call-sites))\n+               (jing/segment-address? (:record call-sites)))\n+      (when-let [tree (stored-tree handle (:yin.module/tree manifest))]\n+        (let [stored-rows (jing/get handle (:table call-sites) nil)\n+              stored-record (jing/get handle (:record call-sites) nil)\n+              origin (:yang.call-site/origin stored-record)]\n+          (when (and (vector? stored-rows)\n+                     (= {:yang.call-site/version 1\n+                         :yang.call-site/root (:yin.module/tree manifest)\n+                         :yang.call-site/table (:table call-sites)}\n+                        (select-keys stored-record\n+                                     [:yang.call-site/version\n+                                      :yang.call-site/root\n+                                      :yang.call-site/table]))\n+                     (vm/occurrence-origin? origin))\n+            {:origin origin, :root (:root tree), :rows stored-rows,\n+             :tree tree}))))))\n+\n+\n ;; =============================================================================\n ;; Deriving a module from indexed code (5.3)\n ;; =============================================================================\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The delta confirms that cc1 adds call-site tables to the hashed manifest and transfers them with the module closure. I’m checking how it constructs those tables and their origins to distinguish an intentional address change from a cross-host mismatch.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,115p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; sed -n '380,455p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|core-module' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc src test/yang/python/antlr/dht*; sed -n '1,200p' src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc; sed -n '1,120p' src/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc; sed -n '175,240p' src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc; rg -n 'ast-side-tables|frontend-metadata' src/cljc/yin/vm\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,115p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; sed -n '380,455p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest|core-module' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc src test/yang/python/antlr/dht*; sed -n '1,200p' src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc; sed -n '1,120p' src/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc; sed -n '175,240p' src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc; rg -n 'ast-side-tables|frontend-metadata' src/cljc/yin/vm\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test\n  \"C4 slices I3/I5 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): Python modules published\n   by name and imported over the DHT.\n\n   The fast tests pin the publication: a unit set publishes bottom-up, a\n   cyclic pair publishes as one SCC bundle step, an import\n   no unit or publication supplies is refused.\n\n   The slow test is the acceptance over the `dao.jing.dht` mesh seam, the\n   in-process form `yin.vm.linker.dht-end-to-end-test` uses, so it runs on\n   the JVM, Node and Dart alike. What travels is the JVM's publication:\n   the artifact `yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture` reads, written on\n   the JVM by its generator script -- the guest blobs, manifest addresses\n   and signed envelopes of `A`'s units and `B`'s name, and the importer\n   packets. No host republishes it: the publisher node serves the\n   artifact's bytes and envelopes as they are. Each host also publishes\n   the same packets itself, into a store of its own, and must arrive at\n   the artifact: a host-specific publication difference fails there.\n   `py` is the runtime every node has installed, one manifest address on\n   every host (`linked-prelude-test`'s golden, and the artifact's), since\n   its code images exceed the DHT's message bound.\n\n   One reader, handed `A`'s index manifest and declaring `A`, imports\n   through the DHT link source on the semantic, stack and register VMs.\n   Then `B` vouches for a module, and the reader, declaring `B` too, is\n   refused it by the default admission interpreter while it trusts only `A`\n   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 7.5), raising ImportError in Python with no install\n   child and no output, and allowed it once it trusts `B`. Next, `B`'s head\n   moves the name to another module between the admission question and its\n   answer: the allow binds the module the question was asked about. Last,\n   `A`'s republication of `k` is indexed, and the reader's import of `t`,\n   which pinned the old `k`, encounters a dependency pin mismatch at\n   statement-time receive when `k` is delivered, raising ImportError before `k`\n   is installed or runs.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.datom :as datom]\n    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    [dao.jing.dht :as jing.dht]\n    [dao.jing.dht.mesh :as mesh]\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    [dao.space.dht-test :as dht-test]\n    [dao.space.index :as index]\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n    [yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture :as fixture]\n    [yang.python.antlr.import-programs :as programs]\n    [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.python.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yang.python.antlr.render :as render]\n    [yang.python.antlr.safepoint :as hooks]\n    [yang.python.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    [yin.vm.linker.admission :as admission]\n    [yin.vm.linker.dht :as ld]\n    [yin.vm.linker.head :as head]\n    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The fast tests: publication order, cycles, admission\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private stand-in-manifest\n  {:yin.module/requires {'yang.call :test/call-address}})\n\n\n(defn- unit\n  [nm pk]\n  {:name nm, :packet pk, :package? false})\n\n\n(deftest units-publish-after-what-they-import-test\n  (testing \"t imports k: k is ordered first whatever the input order\"\n    (is (= {:status :ok, :order [\"k\" \"t\" \"m\"]}\n           (publication/publication-order\n             [(unit \"t\" programs/t-packet) (unit \"k\" programs/k-packet)\n              (unit \"m\" programs/m-packet)]\n             {}))))\n  (testing \"an import a publication already supplies needs no unit\"\n    (is (= {:status :ok, :order [\"t\"]}\n           (publication/publication-order [(unit \"t\" programs/t-packet)]\n                                          {\"k\" :test/k})))))\n\n\n(deftest cyclic-components-are-ordered-as-one-publication-step-test\n  (doseq [units [[(unit \"ca\" programs/ca-packet) (unit \"cb\" programs/cb-packet)]\n                 [(unit \"cb\" programs/cb-packet) (unit \"ca\" programs/ca-packet)]]]\n    (is (= {:status :ok, :order [[\"ca\" \"cb\"]]}\n           (publication/publication-order units {})))))\n\n\n(deftest an-unsupplied-import-is-refused-at-publication-test\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n        py-address (jing/materialize! store stand-in-manifest)\n        before-addresses (set (keys ((:entries-fn store))))]\n    (is (= {:status :refused,\n            :reason :yang.python.antlr/unpublished-import,\n            :module \"k\",\n            :imported-by \"t\"}\n           (publication/publish-units! store (h/registry) py-address\n                                       [(unit \"t\" programs/t-packet)])))\n    (is (= before-addresses\n           (set (keys ((:entries-fn store))))))))\n\n\n;; the artifact's modules as [name manifest]: the units, then k's republication\n(defn- artifact-modules\n                  {:trusted (set (map sign/principal trusted))})}))\n\n\n(defn- on-every-vm\n  \"Thread `w` through `run-over-dht` on every vector backend: `[w {backend\n   [outcome last-response observation]}]`.\"\n  [w pk src]\n  (reduce (fn [[w acc] k]\n            (let [[w outcome response seen] (run-over-dht w k pk src)]\n              [w (assoc acc k [outcome response seen])]))\n          [w {}]\n          (keys h/backends)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The acceptance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- first-difference\n  \"The first key of the artifacts `a` and `b` (`fixture/parse`'s data)\n   whose values differ, with the blob addresses only one holds or holds\n   other bytes at; nil when they are equal.\"\n  [a b]\n  (when (not= a b)\n    (let [blobs (fn [x y]\n                  (sort (map str (remove #(= (get x %) (get y %))\n                                         (keys x)))))]\n      {:keys (vec (sort (map str (filter #(not= (get a %) (get b %))\n                                         (distinct (concat (keys a)\n                                                           (keys b))))))),\n       :blobs-differ (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs a) (:blobs b)))),\n       :blobs-only-here (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs b) (:blobs a))))})))\n\n\n(defn- this-host-publishes-the-artifact\n  [artifact-lines]\n  (testing \"this host's own publication of the committed packets is the\n            JVM's artifact: same manifests, blobs and envelopes\"\n    (let [{:keys [lines refused]} (fixture/generate)]\n      (is (nil? refused) (pr-str refused))\n      (when lines\n        (is (nil? (first-difference (fixture/parse artifact-lines)\n                                    (fixture/parse lines))))))))\n\n\n(defn- publish-world\n  \"Publisher `A` at mesh port 1, plain peers at 2 and 3, a reader at 4,\n   `A` and the reader with `py` installed: `A`'s node serves the\n   artifact's guest blobs as they are and its first index (py, m, k and\n   t named by `A`), which the reader loads.\"\n  [artifact]\n  (let [net (mesh/mesh)\n        installed (fixture/installed-py)\n        pub (node-at net 1 [2 3] true installed)\n        put! (:put-bytes-fn (dht/store pub))\n        w {:net net,\n           :pub pub,\n           :reader (node-at net 4 [2 3 1] false\n                            (merge installed (fixture/installed-pysp))),\n           :peers (into {} (map (fn [p] [p (peer-node net p)])) [2 3]),\n           :now 0,\n           :events []}]\n    (testing \"every node's installed py is the artifact's\"\n      (is (= (:py artifact) (:address @h/published))))\n    (run! (fn [[address bs]] (put! address bs))\n          (sort-by (comp str key) (:blobs artifact)))\n    (first (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :own])))))\n\n\n(def ^:private nothing-ran\n  \"A refused import's observation: no line printed and no guest install\n   child; `yang.call` and `py` are the two runtime install children.\"\n  {:output [], :guests #{}, :children 2})\n\n\n(defn- observes\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:80:(deftest units-publish-after-what-they-import-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:93:(deftest cyclic-components-are-ordered-as-one-publication-step-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:100:(deftest an-unsupplied-import-is-refused-at-publication-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:122:(deftest published-site-sets-verify-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:887:(deftest ^:slow dht-import-test-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:80:(deftest units-publish-after-what-they-import-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:93:(deftest cyclic-components-are-ordered-as-one-publication-step-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:100:(deftest an-unsupplied-import-is-refused-at-publication-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:122:(deftest published-site-sets-verify-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:887:(deftest ^:slow dht-import-test-test\nsrc/dev/jolt_runner_sentinel.clj:9:(deftest before-the-throw\nsrc/dev/jolt_runner_sentinel.clj:13:(deftest throws\nsrc/dev/jolt_runner_sentinel.clj:17:(deftest after-the-throw\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:21:(deftest read-str-values\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:33:(deftest read-str-numbers\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:46:(deftest read-str-strings\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:54:(deftest read-str-unpaired-surrogate-escape\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:62:(deftest read-str-refuses-malformed-input\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:69:(deftest write-str-defaults\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:80:(deftest write-str-review-rows\nsrc/dev/jolt_json_shim_check.cljc:92:(deftest round-trip\nsrc/dev/jolt_j2_manifest_check.clj:11:(deftest manifest-check\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:14:(deftest exact-subsystem-coverage\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:46:(deftest docs-checks-staged-and-untracked\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:85:(deftest routed-verification-scope\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:112:(deftest quick-verification-scope\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:150:(deftest quick-prerequisite-failure-scope\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:172:(deftest summaries-fail-closed\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:187:(deftest bounded-worker-count\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:199:(deftest routing-policy\nsrc/dev/quick_sharded_test.clj:232:(deftest content-cache-invalidation\nsrc/dev/yang/php/oracle_test.clj:14:(deftest uncaught-block-keeps-shutdown-output-test\nsrc/dev/yang/php/oracle_test.clj:29:(deftest plain-fatal-keeps-shutdown-output-test\nsrc/dev/jolt_cbor_override_self_test.clj:15:(deftest override-check\nsrc/dev/jolt_cbor_override_self_test.clj:128:(deftest extraction\nsrc/dev/check_node_discovery_test.clj:9:(deftest node-discovery-check\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:15:(deftest classify-sorts-changed-paths\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:40:(deftest form-deps-reads-every-libspec-shape\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:60:(deftest ns-info-reads-every-reader-conditional-branch\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:81:(deftest path->ns-derives-a-namespace-from-a-path\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:88:(deftest convention-test-paths-maps-src-to-test\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:95:(deftest reverse-closure-follows-dependents-transitively\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:105:(deftest mentions-matches-a-path-or-basename\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:114:(deftest scanner-roots-finds-file-seq-roots\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:122:(deftest scanner-roots-finds-every-walker-shape\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:147:(deftest under-root-matches-a-path-in-a-tree\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:177:(deftest index-entry-marks-test-namespaces\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:186:(deftest select-takes-the-closure-to-test-namespaces\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:220:(deftest lane-tests-filters-by-host\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:229:(deftest ns-regexp-escapes-dots-for-edn\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:233:(deftest parse-summary-reads-each-runner\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:248:(deftest prerequisites-follow-the-forward-closure\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:272:(deftest serialized-pairs-detects-a-jvm-cljd-build\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:305:(deftest select-finds-walkers-of-every-shape\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:314:(deftest parse-args-reads-the-options\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:337:(deftest normalize-path-makes-paths-repo-relative\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:347:(deftest input-errors-refuse-a-vacuous-green\nsrc/dev/affected_test.clj:376:(deftest subsystems-orphan-and-coverage-check\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:45:    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3854:        operands (into [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)] defs)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3866:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3913:        operands (into [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)] defs)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3923:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3974:        ast (core-module/module-tree (concat spec-defs body-defs [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)]))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3975:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3984:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3988:                (core-module/alias-spec (path-module-symbol name) module-exports\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:68:    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:538:  (core-module/module-symbol \"py\" name))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2075:(def ^:private require-node core-module/require-node)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2126:  (core-module/declare-free-name :yang.python.antlr/refusal\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2154:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2165:(def ^:private module-tree core-module/module-tree)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2278:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2289:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2293:                (core-module/alias-spec (module-symbol name) module-exports\n(ns yang.core.call\n  \"Language-neutral guest calling convention (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n   §8.10). This namespace emits the same pure definitions into bundled\n   preludes and the linked `yang.call` module.\"\n  (:require [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module that publishes the shared calling runtime.\"\n  'yang.call)\n\n\n(def host-names\n  \"Host module names read by the guest definitions.\"\n  '#{cell/get cell/authentic? data/callable? data/contains? data/count\n     data/map? data/nth data/string? data/vector?})\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The one ordered definition list used by both emitters.\"\n  '[;; Descriptor projection remains structural after callable admission,\n    ;; with one ruling-of-record refinement: a `:cell-ref`-shaped map is\n    ;; dereferenced only when the heap authenticates it (`cell/authentic?`,\n    ;; the issuer's own answer). A map that imitates the reference language\n    ;; is data, so it projects to itself and its fate follows the ordinary\n    ;; descriptor rules, exactly as any other map's would.\n    [yang.call/_descriptor\n     (fn [callable]\n       (if (data/map? callable)\n         (if (if (= (get callable :type) :cell-ref)\n               (cell/authentic? callable)\n               false)\n           (cell/get callable)\n           callable)\n         nil))]\n    [yang.call/entry\n     (fn [callable]\n       (get (yang.call/_descriptor callable) :yang.call/entry))]\n    [yang.call/eligible?\n     (fn [callable]\n       (let [descriptor (yang.call/_descriptor callable)]\n         (if (nil? (yang.call/entry callable))\n           false\n           (if (data/contains? descriptor :yang.call/eligible?)\n             ((get descriptor :yang.call/eligible?) callable)\n             true))))]\n    [yang.call/invocation\n     (fn [callee positional named raise]\n       (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/callee callee)\n                            :yang.call/positional positional)\n                     :yang.call/named named)\n              :yang.call/raise raise))]\n    [yang.call/invocation-with\n     (fn [callee positional named raise options]\n       (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc options :yang.call/callee callee)\n                            :yang.call/positional positional)\n                     :yang.call/named named)\n              :yang.call/raise raise))]\n    [yang.call/_pair?\n     (fn [pair]\n       (if (data/vector? pair)\n         (= (data/count pair) 2)\n         false))]\n    [yang.call/_named-pairs?\n     (fn [pairs index]\n       (if (= index (data/count pairs))\n         true\n         (let [pair (data/nth pairs index)]\n           (if (yang.call/_pair? pair)\n             (if (data/string? (data/nth pair 0))\n               (yang.call/_named-pairs? pairs (+ index 1))\n               false)\n             false))))]\n    [yang.call/valid-invocation?\n     (fn [invocation]\n       (if (data/map? invocation)\n         (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/callee)\n           (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/positional)\n             (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/named)\n               (if (data/contains? invocation :yang.call/raise)\n                 (if (data/vector? (get invocation :yang.call/positional))\n                   (if (data/vector? (get invocation :yang.call/named))\n                     (yang.call/_named-pairs?\n                       (get invocation :yang.call/named) 0)\n                     false)\n                   false)\n                 false)\n               false)\n             false)\n           false)\n         false))]\n    [yang.call/condition\n     (fn [reason evidence]\n       (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/reason reason)\n              :yang.call/data evidence))]\n    [yang.call/thrown\n     (fn [value]\n       (assoc (assoc {} :yang.call/reason :yang.call/thrown)\n              :yang.call/value value))]\n    [yang.call/transfer\n     (fn [raise condition]\n       (raise condition))]\n    [yang.call/invoke\n     (fn [callable positional named raise]\n       (if (data/callable? raise)\n         (if (yang.call/eligible? callable)\n           (let [target (yang.call/entry callable)\n                 record (yang.call/invocation callable positional named raise)]\n             (if (not (nil? target))\n               (if (yang.call/valid-invocation? record)\n                 (target record)\n                 (yang.call/transfer\n                   raise\n                   (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                        {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n               (yang.call/transfer\n                 raise\n                 (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                      {:yang.call/callee callable}))))\n           (yang.call/transfer\n             raise\n             (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable\n                                  {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n         (raise (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                     {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}))))]\n    [yang.call/invoke-with\n     (fn [callable positional named raise options]\n       (if (data/callable? raise)\n         (if (yang.call/eligible? callable)\n           (let [target (yang.call/entry callable)\n                 record (yang.call/invocation-with\n                          callable positional named raise options)]\n             (if (not (nil? target))\n               (if (yang.call/valid-invocation? record)\n                 (target record)\n                 (yang.call/transfer\n                   raise\n                   (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                        {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n               (yang.call/transfer\n                 raise\n                 (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                      {:yang.call/callee callable}))))\n           (yang.call/transfer\n             raise\n             (yang.call/condition :yang.call/not-callable\n                                  {:yang.call/callee callable})))\n         (raise (yang.call/condition :yang.call/invalid-invocation\n                                     {:yang.call/reason :missing-raise-exit}))))]])\n\n\n(def ^:private public-exports\n  '#{entry eligible? invocation invocation-with valid-invocation? condition\n     thrown transfer invoke invoke-with})\n\n\n(def uast\n  \"The bundled definitions, in source order and tail marked.\"\n  (u/mark-tails\n    (reduce (fn [ast [key form]]\n              (u/then ast (u/def! key (u/sexp->uast form))))\n            (u/def! (ffirst definitions)\n                    (u/sexp->uast (second (first definitions))))\n            (rest definitions))))\n\n\n(def module-uast\n  \"The linked module tree built from the same `definitions`. C1\n   finalized, like every published production tree: its\n   `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside its manifest (see\n   `yin.vm.linker.publish`).\"\n  (let [stripped (core/module-definitions \"yang.call\" :yang.call/uninit\n                                          [] definitions)]\n    (u/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree stripped []))))\n\n\n(def module-exports\n  \"Public module exports (private helper definitions stay internal).\"\n  public-exports)\n\n\n(def ^:private module-free-names\n  (core/free-name-vec module-uast))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"The linker module spec for `yang.call` over `registry`.\"\n  [registry]\n  (core/module-spec {:module-name module-name\n                     :ast module-uast\n                     :exports module-exports\n                     :requires {}\n                     :free-names module-free-names\n                     :registry registry\n                     :message \"the yang.call module reads an undeclared name\"\n                     :refusal-ns \"yang.call\"}))\n(ns yang.core.module\n  \"Module emitter machinery shared by every language frontend\n   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md §17, lift L3): the linker module naming\n   rule, the `require` and wide-application tree nodes, free-name\n   declaration over a host registry, and the `module-spec` and SCC bundle\n   shapes `yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!` takes. A language supplies\n   its prefix, its runtime module and its module AST; nothing here knows a\n   source language.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [yang.core.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(defn module-symbol\n  \"The linker module name of source module `name` under language `prefix`\n   (\\\"py\\\", \\\"php\\\", \\\"js\\\"): `<prefix>m.` then the name with each dot a `$`,\n   so no linker module name is a dotted prefix of another.\"\n  [prefix name]\n  (symbol (str prefix \"m.\" (str/replace name \".\" \"$\"))))\n\n\n(defn require-node\n  \"(require 'm) as a tree node.\"\n  [m]\n  (u/sexp->uast (list 'require (list 'quote m))))\n\n\n(defn module-tree\n  \"A wide application: all definitions remain at module level.\"\n  [operands]\n  (prelude/wide-app operands))\n\n\n(defn declare-free-name\n  \"The `:primitives` entry free name `n` declares over `registry`, or nil\n   when `covered` (the requirement-pinned module names) covers it. A name\n   no `vm/primitives` profile or host export supplies throws, with\n   `refusal` under `refusal-key` in its data.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry covered n]\n  (if (and (symbol? n) (some? (namespace n))\n           (contains? covered (symbol (namespace n))))\n    nil\n    (if-let [profile (vm/profile-of vm/primitives n)]\n      [n profile]\n      (if-let [address (module/host-export-profile registry n)]\n        (let [entry (module/module-entry (:modules registry)\n                                         (symbol (namespace n)))\n              f (get-in entry [:slice (symbol (name n))])]\n          [n {:yin.k/profile address,\n              :yin.k/effects\n              (get (:callable-effects registry) f #{})}])\n        (throw (ex-info \"the module reads an undeclared name\"\n                        {refusal-key refusal, :name n}))))))\n\n\n(defn free-primitives\n  \"The `:primitives` map declaring every free name of `ast` over `registry`.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry covered ast]\n  (let [free (remove (conj (prelude/defined-keys ast) 'yin/def)\n                     (prelude/free-names ast))]\n    (into {}\n          (keep (partial declare-free-name refusal-key refusal registry covered))\n          (sort-by str free))))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"`publish-module!`'s spec for module `name`: `ast` with `exports`, requiring\n   the runtime module `runtime-name` at `runtime-address` and each of `deps`\n   ({module-symbol address}). A free name under a required module is covered\n   by it; any other is declared as `declare-free-name` does.\"\n  [refusal-key refusal registry\n   {:keys [name ast exports runtime-name runtime-address deps]}]\n  (let [requires (into {runtime-name runtime-address} deps)]\n    {:name name,\n     :ast ast,\n     :exports exports,\n     :requires requires,\n     :primitives (free-primitives refusal-key refusal registry\n                                  (set (keys requires)) ast)}))\n\n\n(defn alias-spec\n  \"A thin member alias of the SCC bundle `bundle-name`: it requires the\n   bundle and defines `spec` and `body` as the bundle's `spec-key` and\n   `body-key` exports.\"\n  [name exports require-profile bundle-name spec-key body-key]\n  {:name name,\n   :exports exports,\n   :primitives {'require require-profile},\n   :ast (module-tree\n          [(require-node bundle-name)\n           (u/def! 'spec (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str spec-key))))\n           (u/def! 'body (u/v (symbol (str bundle-name) (str body-key))))])})\n\n\n(defn scc-module-specs\n  \"The SCC publication shape: the `bundle` spec first, then the member alias\n   specs (each `alias-spec`'s output) in member order.\"\n  [bundle aliases]\n  (into [bundle] aliases))\n             (= :literal (:type (first operands)))\n             (symbol? (:value (first operands))))\n    (:value (first operands))))\n\n\n(defn- ast-children\n  \"`[[path-suffix child] ...]` of one AST node in grammar order. A suffix\n   holds one coordinate: the full-row position of a `node` slot or\n   `[position i]` of a `nodes` child, as in its canonical row (§2.1).\"\n  [node]\n  (apply concat\n         (map-indexed (fn [i [field kind]]\n                        (let [pos (+ i 2)]\n                          (case kind\n                            :node [[[pos] (get node field)]]\n                            :nodes (map-indexed (fn [k c] [[[pos k]] c])\n                                                (get node field))\n                            nil)))\n                      (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (:type node)))))\n\n\n(defn- declaration-order\n  \"§3.5's declaration order for one node's children: for an application\n   whose operator is a lambda, the operands left to right and then the\n   lambda body (two coordinates below the application); otherwise grammar\n   order.\"\n  [node]\n  (let [places (ast-children node)]\n    (if (and (= :application (:type node)) (= :lambda (:type (:operator node))))\n      (concat (rest places) [[[2 3] (:body (:operator node))]])\n      places)))\n\n\n(defn- definition-occurrences\n  \"Every definition occurrence of one member AST as `{:path p :declared? b}`,\n   in source declaration order. A declared occurrence is one whose value is\n   a lambda the frontend flagged `:macro?`.\"\n  [ast]\n  (letfn [(walk [node path]\n            (concat (when (definition-name node)\n                      [{:path path,\n                        :declared? (boolean (:macro? (second (:operands node))))}])\n                    (mapcat (fn [[suffix child]] (walk child (into path suffix)))\n                            (declaration-order node))))]\n    (vec (walk ast []))))\n\n\n(defn- member-ast\n  [member]\n  (cond (and (map? member) (contains? member :type)) member\n        (sequential? member) (vm/datoms->ast (vec member))\n        :else (throw (ex-info \"Unsupported program batch member\"\n                              {:rule :batch-member, :member member}))))\n\n\n(def ^:private call-site-key\n  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence\n   contract C1 (`yang.clojure`), enforced at this boundary but not\n   owned by it.\"\n  :yang/call-site)\n\n\n(defn- marked-call-sites\n  \"The `[path value]` of every node of map AST `ast` carrying the C1\n   key, walked by the row grammar. Literal payloads are data, never\n   syntax, and are not walked. Member ASTs are already projected by the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:109:             (vm/ast-side-tables member tree origin)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:112:    {:tree member, :source-positions [], :frontend-metadata [],\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:121:             (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:147:           :yin/frontend-metadata (into [] (mapcat :frontend-metadata) projected)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:231:  \"The reserved frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:98:;; every final `:application` occurrence) publishes its frontend-metadata\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:198:                            (:frontend-metadata\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:199:                              (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1600:   final tree, as frontend-metadata rows `[origin root path\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1635:   carries `:frontend-metadata` — the C1 side table finalized over the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1665:                      :frontend-metadata (:frontend-metadata st),\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1743:                                 :frontend-metadata metadata\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1863:   side table (the batch result's `:frontend-metadata`, present only\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1872:  (let [{:keys [status tree log error ctx frontend-metadata\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1877:      (and (= :ok status) frontend-metadata)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:1879:                frontend-metadata)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
