{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn.*ast-side-tables|core-module|keyword\\\\?|namespace|keyword ' src/cljc/dao/datom.cljc src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc; sed -n '1,160p' test/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc; sed -n '1,190p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc; sed -n '875,930p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc; rg -n 'Call-site occurrence|admission identity|call-site.*contract|origin.*publication' docs/design\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:353:    {:yin.k/profile (keyword \"yin.k.pp\" (str \"blake3-\" digest)),\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:528:  (or (keyword? x)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:537:  (or (keyword? x)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:541:           (keyword? (nth x 1)))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:631:   :yin/type {},      ; keyword (:literal, :variable, :lambda, ...)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:634:   :yin/op {},        ; keyword (dao.stream.apply operation key)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:662:   :yin.code/type {},      ; keyword (:segment)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:666:   :yin.code/op {},        ; keyword mnemonic (:const, :call, :halt, ...)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:675:   :yin.code/ffi-op {},    ; keyword (dao.stream.apply operation key)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:909:                     (keyword? x) (symbol? x))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:929:                       (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1192:                   :when (and (= \"yang\" (namespace k))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1217:(defn ast-side-tables\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1271:    :kw (keyword? v)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1907:                  (when (and (namespace n)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1911:                                                    (str (namespace n) \".\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:3:   and P3, docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): the namespace that requires\nsrc/cljc/dao/datom.cljc:9:   This namespace is the single source of truth for the reserved ids and for\nsrc/cljc/dao/datom.cljc:32:   and v slots as namespaced keywords, already globally meaningful without an\nsrc/cljc/dao/datom.cljc:45:   `t`, integer `m`, and a namespaced keyword attribute. Negative tempids are\nsrc/cljc/dao/datom.cljc:53:       (keyword? (nth x 1))\nsrc/cljc/dao/datom.cljc:54:       (some? (namespace (nth x 1)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:8:   and the rulings in its README; this namespace implements it, it does not\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:15:     over `[namespace name]`, read from the identifier's fields;\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:34:   corpus refusal classes as a keyword (`:non-canonical`,\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:82:  \"The refusal class keyword of a thrown codec refusal, or nil. A refusal\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:414:  [(if (keyword? x) :keyword :symbol) (namespace x) (name x)])\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:438:    (or (keyword? x) (symbol? x)) (hash (identifier-key x))\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:453:   identifiers by their namespace and name fields, lists equal to vectors\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:462:    (or (keyword? a) (symbol? a))\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:463:    (and (or (keyword? b) (symbol? b))\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:543:   namespace and name fields, lists and vectors alike (README ruling A6)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:554:    (or (keyword? x) (symbol? x)) [::identifier (identifier-key x)]\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:852:        ns (namespace x)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:892:    (keyword? x) (identifier-bytes \"dao.jing/keyword\" x d)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:1161:        (refuse :malformed-frame \"namespace is neither nil nor text\"))\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:1166:          (keyword ns (:value name-item))\n(ns yang.python.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the Python tests (C4 slices P2\n   and P3, docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): the namespace that requires\n   this is the publisher of `py` and `pysp`, so it publishes each module\n   once per process into one in-memory content store and serves them to\n   every linked run over a `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under\n   `:trusted` derivation (the remediation ruling's R6). The `:verifying`\n   evidence is `publish-module!`'s own `link-local` links, which\n   `linked-prelude-test` asserts.\n\n   A linked run builds the program's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately\n   until the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker\n   is not a backend here: its link of `py` is refused `:undeclared-free`\n   until L-b.\"\n  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n            [yang.core.call :as call]\n            [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.python.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def integer-limits\n  \"The ordinary Python composition's `integer` limits.\"\n  {::integer/max-bits 100000, ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The full host registry a linked Python composition registers: the\n   `require` handler, then `cell`, `data`, `integer` under `limits`, and\n   `stream` — the hook module `pysp` polls a signal stream, so the\n   safepointed composition needs it even though `py` does not.\"\n  ([] (registry integer-limits))\n  ([limits]\n   (-> (module/default-registry)\n       module/register-cell-module\n       (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n       (prelude/register-integer-module limits)\n       module/register-stream-module)))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`yang.call` and `py` published once into their own content store.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n          call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n          result (publish/publish-module! store\n                                          (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                               (:address call-result)))]\n      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result),\n       :call-result call-result, :call-address (:address call-result)})))\n\n\n(def published-pysp\n  \"`pysp` published once into `py`'s own content store, which its pinned\n   requirement already lives in: the same shape as `published`.\"\n  (delay\n    (let [{:keys [store address]} @published\n          result (publish/publish-module!\n                   store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) address))]\n      {:store store, :result result, :address (:address result)})))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The serving composition over the published store: `name-env` defaults\n   to `{py <address> yang.call <address>}`, derivation `:trusted`, the test being the\n   publisher. Explicit name environments also receive the harness's\n   `yang.call` runtime module, which every linked Python body requires.\n   `pysp`-serving sources pass their own `name-env`, the\n   safepointed runs' `{'py a :pysp b}` both.\"\n  ([] (source {'py (:address @published),\n               'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n  ([name-env]\n   (link/composition {:content-store (:store @published),\n                      :name-env (merge {'yang.call (:call-address @published)}\n                                       name-env),\n                      :derivation :trusted})))\n\n\n(defn safepoint-source\n  \"The serving composition for `pysp`, `py`, and the `yang.call` module\n   required by `py`.\"\n  []\n  (source {'py (:address @published), 'pysp (:address @published-pysp),\n           'yang.call (:call-address @published)}))\n\n\n(defn publish-guest-module!\n  \"One guest module's `spec` (lower/module-spec's) published into `py`'s\n   own content store, where its pinned requirements already live:\n   `publish-module!`'s answer. The test helper supplies the harness's\n   `yang.call` address as the runtime dependency when a test constructs a\n   spec directly. Guest modules are tiny beside `py`, so a test may publish\n   its own; publish imports bottom-up, the `deps` map naming each import's\n   address.\"\n  [spec]\n  (publish/publish-module! (:store @published)\n                           (update spec :requires\n                                   #(assoc (or % {}) 'yang.call\n                                           (:call-address @published)))))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n   :register (fn [ast opts]\n               (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                              (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract)))})\n\n\n(def continues\n  \"Each vector backend's admission of the next top-level unit to a halted\n   task, as `yin.repl` admits an input line: the task keeps its store,\n   heap, module registry and module stores.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [task ast]\n               (semantic/load-ast task (vm/ast->datoms ast) vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [task ast]\n            (let [img (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                  attached (dvm/attach-image task img vm/stack-contract)]\n              (assoc attached\n                     :pc (dvm/absolute-pc attached [(dcode/image-hash img) 0])\n                     :frames [] :stack [] :continuation []\n                     :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil))),\n   :register (fn [task ast]\n               (let [img (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                     attached (rvm/attach-image task img vm/register-contract)\n                     pc (rvm/absolute-pc attached\n                                         [(rcode/register-hash img) 0])\n                     body (some #(when (= pc (:start %)) %)\n                                (:bodies (:segment attached)))]\n                 (assoc attached\n                        :pc pc :frames [] :continuation []\n                        :registers (vec (repeat (:registers body) nil))\n                        :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)))})\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"A task's composition over `modules` and the link `pair`.\"\n  [modules pair]\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n(ns yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture\n  \"The JVM publication artifact of C4 slice I3's DHT import\n   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): test/resources/yang/python/\n   dht-import-v1.edn, written on the JVM by\n   test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.generate.clj.\n\n   It holds what a publisher `A` publishes and signs: the guest blobs of\n   the units m, k, t and e and of k's republication k2 (every blob of\n   their closures but `py`'s, which each reader has installed, and each\n   module's site set blob and publication record blob, I7), each\n   unit's manifest address, the signed name envelopes of three index\n   transactions -- `A` naming py, yang.call, m, k and t; `A` retracting k and\n   naming k2; a foreign principal `B` naming e -- and the importer\n   packets the reader lowers, and a fourth index transaction of `A`'s signed\n   site-set publication entries (I7). The keys are fixed test seeds, and Ed25519\n   signatures are deterministic, so one host's `generate` is the file\n   byte for byte.\n\n   `yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test` consumes the file on every host\n   without republishing anything, and checks that this host's own\n   `generate` equals it: a host whose publication of the same packets\n   differs from the JVM's fails there.\n\n   One EDN form per line: the magic, the header maps, then one\n   `[address hex]` line per blob in address order.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as cfx]\n    [dao.jing.dht :as jing.dht]\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [yang.python.antlr.import-programs :as programs]\n    [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.python.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yang.python.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    [yin.vm.linker.closure :as closure]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n\n\n(def path\n  \"The artifact, relative to the repository root.\"\n  \"test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn\")\n\n\n(def magic \"dht-import-v1\")\n\n\n(def key-a\n  \"The publisher `A`: a fixed test seed.\"\n  (let [seed (apply str (repeat 32 \"a1\"))]\n    {:seed seed, :public (sign/public-of seed)}))\n\n\n(def key-b\n  \"The foreign principal `B`: a fixed test seed.\"\n  (let [seed (apply str (repeat 32 \"b2\"))]\n    {:seed seed, :public (sign/public-of seed)}))\n\n\n(defn closure-addresses\n  \"Every blob address of the closure of `manifest` in `store`: the reads\n   one closure walk makes.\"\n  [store manifest]\n  (let [seen (atom #{})\n        get-bytes (:get-bytes-fn store)\n        recording (assoc store\n                         :get-bytes-fn\n                         (fn [address not-found]\n                           (swap! seen conj address)\n                           (get-bytes address not-found)))]\n    (closure/walk recording manifest)\n    @seen))\n\n\n(defn installed-py\n  \"`py`'s closure as this host published it, `{address bytes}`: the\n   Python runtime every reader has installed. It does not travel: three\n   of its blobs (the code images, about 1 MB each) exceed the DHT's\n   64 KiB message bound, which a `dao.space.dht` node does not let a\n   composition raise.\"\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [store address]} @h/published]\n    (select-keys ((:entries-fn store)) (closure-addresses store address))))\n\n\n(defn installed-pysp\n  \"`pysp`'s closure as this host published it, `{address bytes}`: the hook\n   runtime a reader under a hook profile has installed, as it has `py`\n   (the closure includes `py`'s).\"\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [store]} @h/published\n        pysp (:address @h/published-pysp)\n        addresses (closure-addresses store pysp)]\n    (select-keys ((:entries-fn store)) addresses)))\n\n\n(defn- unit\n  [nm pk]\n  {:name nm, :packet pk, :package? false})\n\n\n(defn- assert-names\n  \"`key`'s assertions binding each `[module address]` of `bound`, at\n   consecutive sequences from `seq0`.\"\n  [key seq0 bound]\n  (vec (map-indexed (fn [i [n a]]\n                      (publish/assertion key {:name n,\n                                              :manifest a,\n                                              :seq (+ seq0 i)}))\n                    bound)))\n\n\n(defn- signed-only\n  [signed]\n  (mapv #(select-keys % [:envelope :proof]) signed))\n\n\n(defn generate\n  \"This host's artifact: the units published from the committed packets\n   into a store holding `py` as this host published it, `A`'s and `B`'s\n   envelopes signed over the addresses. Answers `{:lines [...]}`, or the\n   first publication refusal as `{:refused r}`.\"\n  []\n  (let [py (:address @h/published)\n        installed (installed-py)\n        store (mem/create-content-mem installed)\n        units (publication/publish-units!\n                store (h/registry) py\n                [(unit \"m\" programs/m-packet) (unit \"k\" programs/k-packet)\n                 (unit \"t\" programs/t-packet) (unit \"e\" programs/e-packet)])\n        k2 (publication/publish-units! store (h/registry) py\n                                       [(unit \"k\" programs/k2-packet)])]\n    (if-let [refused (some #(when (not= :ok (:status %)) %) [units k2])]\n      {:refused refused}\n      (let [addresses (:addresses units)\n            own (assert-names key-a 1 [['py py]\n                                       ['yang.call (:call-address @h/published)]\n                                       ['pym.m (get addresses \"m\")]\n                                       ['pym.k (get addresses \"k\")]\n                                       ['pym.t (get addresses \"t\")]])\n            republish [(publish/retraction\n                         key-a\n                         {:of (jing/segment-key (:envelope (nth own 3))),\n                          :seq 6})\n                       (publish/assertion\n                         key-a\n                         {:name 'pym.k,\n                          :manifest (get-in k2 [:addresses \"k\"]),\n                          :seq 7})]\n            foreign (assert-names key-b 1 [['pym.e (get addresses \"e\")]])\n            ;; I7: A's signed publication entry for each module's site-set\n            ;; record, the units' then k's republication\n            sites (into []\n                        (mapcat #(siteset/signed-entries\n                                   key-a (:sites %) (:addresses %)\n                                   (:bundles %)))\n                        [units k2])\n            blobs (sort-by (comp str key)\n                           (remove (fn [[a _]] (contains? installed a))\n                                   ((:entries-fn store))))]\n        {:lines\n         (into [magic\n                (pr-str {:py py})\n                (pr-str {:principals {:a (:public key-a),\n                                      :b (:public key-b)}})\n                (pr-str {:units addresses,\n                         :republished {\"k\" (get-in k2 [:addresses \"k\"])}})\n                (pr-str {:importers {:d programs/d-packet,\n                                     :tt programs/tt-packet,\n                                     :x programs/x-packet}})\n                (pr-str {:index :own, :signed (signed-only own)})\n                (pr-str {:index :republish, :signed (signed-only republish)})\n                (pr-str {:index :foreign, :signed (signed-only foreign)})\n                (pr-str {:index :sites, :signed sites})]\n               (map (fn [[a bs]] (pr-str [a (jing.dht/bytes->hex bs)])))\n               blobs)}))))\n\n\n(defn text\n  \"The artifact text of `lines`: one per line, newline terminated.\"\n  [lines]\n  (str (str/join \"\\n\" lines) \"\\n\"))\n\n\n(defn read-lines\n  \"The artifact's lines, blank ones dropped (Dart keeps a trailing one).\"\n  []\n  (vec (remove str/blank? (str/split-lines (cfx/read-path path)))))\n        w (a-hook-import-chain w artifact)\n        w (imports-over-the-dht w artifact src)\n        w (an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm w artifact)\n        w (a-trusted-principal-is-allowed-on-every-vm w artifact)\n        w (an-allow-binds-the-address-the-question-was-asked-about\n            w artifact)\n        w (republished-dependency-is-refused w artifact src)]\n    (dht/close! (:pub w))\n    (dht/close! (:reader w))\n    (an-absent-record-is-refused-and-retried)))\n\n\n(deftest ^:slow dht-import-test-test\n  (slow/guard \"dht-import-test\" dht-import-test))\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:13:> admission identity. H remains a *value*: the integrity checksum of the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:220:> derivation output, pin, or admission identity, in §3, §4 (the pipeline\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.targets.md:9:> pin, dependency or admission identity); R and H remain integrity\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:407:the original publication's ledger (section 5.5).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2015:An exclusive running, blocked or parked root carries policy, occurrence, arbitration and next-op-seq, with origin on a successor; a halted exclusive root carries origin only. A completed `:put` wake is a completed operation: its op-id is well-formed but not a retained write. Completed outcomes never acquire publication or execution authority from their history.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,120p' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc; sed -n '830,885p' src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc; sed -n '1,200p' src/cljc/dao/datom.cljc; rg -n 'ast-side-tables|core-module' src/cljc test/dao/stream/*corpus*; /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/git diff f4df9893 b1b9abae -- src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.jing.cbor\n  \"DaoJing's canonical CBOR value codec and portable numeric operations\n   (docs/design/dao.jing.cbor.md, phases J1 and J2; portable writer in slice H4).\n\n   `encode` turns one supported value into its canonical payload bytes;\n   `decode` accepts exactly one canonical payload and returns its value.\n   The byte contract is the frozen corpus test/resources/dao/jing/cbor-v1.json\n   and the rulings in its README; this namespace implements it, it does not\n   define it.\n\n   Encoding normalizes a value and directly emits canonical CBOR bytes over\n   `dao.host.*`:\n\n   * keywords and symbols: tag 27 `dao.jing/keyword` / `dao.jing/symbol`\n     over `[namespace name]`, read from the identifier's fields;\n   * lists and finite seqs: tag 27 `dao.jing/list` over the item array;\n     vectors are plain arrays;\n   * floating point: tag 27 `dao.jing/float64` over eight big-endian bytes,\n     float32 widened exactly, every NaN made 7ff8000000000000;\n   * integers: CBOR integers, tags 2/3 beyond 64 bits;\n   * decimals: tag 4 `[exponent mantissa]`; ratios: tag 30, reduced;\n   * sets: tag 258 over elements sorted by their canonical bytes;\n   * metadata on collections and symbols: tag 27 `clojure/with-meta` over\n     `[meta value]`, outermost, after stripping unqualified :line :column\n     :end-line :end-column (validated before stripping) and omitting empty\n     metadata.\n\n   Decoding reads the bytes with Jing's own structural reader, which checks\n   every tag, frame name and payload shape before any host conversion (the\n   plan's \\\"validate before any lossy host conversion\\\"), then requires the\n   decoded value to re-encode to the identical bytes.\n\n   Every refusal is an ex-info whose data carries `::refusal`, one of the\n   corpus refusal classes as a keyword (`:non-canonical`,\n   `:unpaired-surrogate`, ...); `refusal` reads it.\n\n   Numbers: the JVM keeps its native exact kinds (long, BigInt, Double,\n   BigDecimal, Ratio) and adds a `Rational` carrier for denominator-1\n   ratios. ClojureScript uses safe-integer numbers and BigInt for integers,\n   and carriers for float64, decimal and rational content. Host `=` cannot\n   compare carriers with native numbers symmetrically, so the portable\n   operations are explicit functions: `num=`, `num-hash`, `num-compare`, and\n   the recursive `equiv` / `equiv-hash`.\n\n   Host contact goes through the primitive profile\n   (docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md §4.2, slice H2): big\n   integers through `dao.host.integer`, the Float64, Decimal and Rational\n   carriers through `dao.host.number`, float bits and fields through\n   `dao.host.float`, byte arrays through `dao.host.bytes` and strict\n   UTF-8 through `dao.host.text`; a profile refusal is answered as this\n   codec's refusal of the same class.\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [decimal? ratio?])\n  (:require\n    [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    [dao.host.float :as float]\n    [dao.host.integer :as integer]\n    [dao.host.number :as number]\n    [dao.host.text :as text]))\n\n\n;; ==========================================================================\n;; Refusals\n;; ==========================================================================\n\n(defn- refuse\n  \"Throw the refusal `cls` (a corpus refusal class keyword).\"\n  ([cls] (refuse cls nil))\n  ([cls detail]\n   (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.jing.cbor refused: \" (name cls)\n                        (when detail (str \" (\" detail \")\")))\n                   {::refusal cls :detail detail}))))\n\n\n(defn- type-name\n  \"The host type of x, for refusal details.\"\n  [x]\n  #?(:cljd (str (.-runtimeType x))\n     :default (str (type x))))\n\n\n(defn refusal\n  \"The refusal class keyword of a thrown codec refusal, or nil. A refusal\n   the `dao.host` profile throws outside any codec call (on JS, the\n   `Float64` carrier refusing implicit numeric coercion) carries the same\n   corpus class under `:dao.host/refusal` and reads the same here.\"\n  [ex]\n  (let [d (ex-data ex)]\n    (or (::refusal d) (:dao.host/refusal d))))\n\n\n(defn- host\n  \"(f & args) through the primitive profile: a `dao.host` refusal comes\n   back as this codec's refusal of the same class (the profile reuses the\n   corpus refusal vocabulary).\"\n  [f & args]\n  (try\n    (apply f args)\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n      (if-let [cls (:dao.host/refusal (ex-data e))]\n        (refuse cls (:detail (ex-data e)))\n        (throw e)))))\n\n\n;; ==========================================================================\n;; Exact host big integers (dao.host.integer)\n;; ==========================================================================\n\n(defn- big\n  \"An exact host big integer from an exact-integer carrier or decimal\n   text (`dao.host.integer/parse-decimal`'s grammar). Anything else (a\n   float, a non-integral number) is refused loudly rather than\n   truncated.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond (integer/exact-integer? x) (integer/promote x)\n        (string? x) (host integer/parse-decimal x)\n        :else (refuse :unsupported-value\n                      (str \"not an exact integer: \" (type-name x)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private zero (integer/from-native 0))\n            (refuse :malformed-frame \"metadata map carries metadata\"))\n          (doseq [k reader-position-keys\n                  :when (contains? m k)]\n            (value-bytes (get m k) (+ d 3)))\n          (let [kept (apply dissoc m reader-position-keys)]\n            (if (empty? kept)\n              (build d)\n              (let [name-bytes (host text/utf8-encode \"clojure/with-meta\")\n                    mb (map-bytes kept (+ d 2))\n                    vb (build (+ d 2))\n                    frame-arr (concat-buffers [(write-head 4 2)\n                                               (write-head 3 (bytes/length name-bytes))\n                                               name-bytes\n                                               (concat-buffers [(write-head 4 2) mb vb])])]\n                (concat-buffers [(write-head 6 27) frame-arr]))))))))\n\n\n(defn- identifier-bytes\n  \"Tag 27 at depth d over [name [ns name]]: the components at d+3.\"\n  [tag-name-str x d]\n  (deep! (+ d 3) :unsupported-value)\n  (let [tag-name-bytes (host text/utf8-encode tag-name-str)\n        ns (namespace x)\n        ns-bytes (if-some [ns-str ns]\n                   (let [ub (host text/utf8-encode (check-text ns-str))]\n                     (concat-buffers [(write-head 3 (bytes/length ub)) ub]))\n                   (bytes/from-vector [0xf6]))\n        name-str (check-text (name x))\n        name-ub (host text/utf8-encode name-str)\n        name-bytes (concat-buffers [(write-head 3 (bytes/length name-ub)) name-ub])\n        inner-arr (concat-buffers [(write-head 4 2) ns-bytes name-bytes])\n        frame-arr (concat-buffers [(write-head 4 2)\n                                   (write-head 3 (bytes/length tag-name-bytes))\n                                   tag-name-bytes\n                                   inner-arr])]\n    (concat-buffers [(write-head 6 27) frame-arr])))\n\n\n(defn- list-bytes\n  \"Tag 27 at depth d over [\\\"dao.jing/list\\\" items]: items at d+3.\"\n  [x d]\n  (deep! (+ d 2) :unsupported-value)\n  (let [tag-name-bytes (host text/utf8-encode \"dao.jing/list\")\n        items (mapv #(value-bytes % (+ d 3)) x)\n        items-arr (concat-buffers (cons (write-head 4 (count items)) items))\n        frame-arr (concat-buffers [(write-head 4 2)\n                                   (write-head 3 (bytes/length tag-name-bytes))\n                                   tag-name-bytes\n                                   items-arr])]\n    (concat-buffers [(write-head 6 27) frame-arr])))\n\n\n(defn- value-bytes\n  \"The canonical CBOR bytes of one value whose outermost item sits at depth d,\n   or a refusal.\"\n  [x d]\n(ns dao.datom\n  \"Reserved metadata-entity ids for the d5 m slot (validity + provenance).\n\n   In a (e a v t m) datom, m is a metadata-entity reference. Low reserved ids\n   mirror Datomic's `added` boolean and extend it; ids at `first-user-id` and\n   above reference reified metadata entities that carry :db/op and provenance\n   as their own datoms.\n\n   This namespace is the single source of truth for the reserved ids and for\n   the boundary between reserved and user space; nothing should compare m or e\n   against a bare literal. See docs/design/datom.md.\")\n\n\n(def reserved\n  \"Reserved metadata-entity ids (ident -> id) for the m slot.\n   0/1 mirror Datomic's `added` boolean; 2 extends it.\"\n  {:db/retract 0, ; added=false\n   :db/assert 1,  ; added=true (emit default)\n   :db/derived 2})  ; computed/derived; excluded from content hash\n\n\n(def default-op\n  \"The m written for emitted datoms when no metadata is supplied: assertion.\"\n  (:db/assert reserved))\n\n\n(def first-user-id\n  \"Lowest entity id available to user entities; 0 through 15 are reserved.\n\n   The block is 16 wide rather than 1024 because only the m-slot markers need\n   globally fixed numbers. Built-in attributes and type markers live in the a\n   and v slots as namespaced keywords, already globally meaningful without an\n   id, and a schema entity in e position takes an ordinary stream-local id\n   named across streams by its :db/ident. Reserving more would put global\n   coordinates in a slot the spec declares a stream-local gauge, and would put\n   the floor above what an int8-wide e can represent at all.\n\n   See docs/design/datom.md, Reserved Entities.\"\n  16)\n\n\n(defn local-datom?\n  \"True for the runtime-enforced portion of a persisted local d5 datom:\n   `[e a v t m]`, with non-negative integer stream-local coordinates `e` and\n   `t`, integer `m`, and a namespaced keyword attribute. Negative tempids are\n   compilation values and must be resolved before commitment. Canonical value\n   encoding is a separate persistence concern and is not decided here.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (vector? x)\n       (= 5 (count x))\n       (integer? (nth x 0))\n       (not (neg? (nth x 0)))\n       (keyword? (nth x 1))\n       (some? (namespace (nth x 1)))\n       (integer? (nth x 3))\n       (not (neg? (nth x 3)))\n       (integer? (nth x 4))))\n\n\n(defn op\n  \"The m (metadata/op) slot of a datom (a [e a v t m] vector or a Datom record).\"\n  [datom]\n  (if (map? datom) (:m datom) (nth datom 4)))\n\n\n(defn asserted?\n  [datom]\n  (= (op datom) (:db/assert reserved)))\n\n\n(defn retracted?\n  [datom]\n  (= (op datom) (:db/retract reserved)))\n\n\n(defn derived?\n  [datom]\n  (= (op datom) (:db/derived reserved)))\n\n\n(def markers\n  \"The reserved op/derived marker ids. These are validity/derivation flags, not\n   references to real metadata entities.\"\n  (set (vals reserved)))\n\n\n(defn metadata-ref?\n  \"True when m references a real metadata entity (not a bare validity/derived\n   marker). Datoms satisfying this belong in the MEAVT index.\"\n  [datom]\n  (not (contains? markers (op datom))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:109:             (vm/ast-side-tables member tree origin)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:121:             (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1217:(defn ast-side-tables\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:52:;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\nsrc/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:260:        tables (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:199:                              (vm/ast-side-tables ast tree origin)))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:45:    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3854:        operands (into [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)] defs)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3866:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3913:        operands (into [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)] defs)\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3923:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3974:        ast (core-module/module-tree (concat spec-defs body-defs [(core-module/require-node prelude/module-name)]))\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3975:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3984:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc:3988:                (core-module/alias-spec (path-module-symbol name) module-exports\nsrc/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc:117:;; as a plain node key. Projection (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:68:    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:538:  (core-module/module-symbol \"py\" name))\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2075:(def ^:private require-node core-module/require-node)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2126:  (core-module/declare-free-name :yang.python.antlr/refusal\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2154:  (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2165:(def ^:private module-tree core-module/module-tree)\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2278:        bundle (core-module/module-spec\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2289:    (core-module/scc-module-specs\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc:2293:                (core-module/alias-spec (module-symbol name) module-exports\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\nindex 30efcd0a..f203b2ca 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc\n@@ -166,10 +